Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: observe ETSI off-channel CAC minimum on 52-64

The MT7986 adjacent receiver checks the 52-64 80 MHz DFS block while
the AP transmits on 36-48. This is off-channel CAC, for which ETSI
EN 301 893 requires at least six minutes (rather than the 60-second
in-channel CAC default). Keep the restriction narrow to this adjacent
prototype's block so unrelated devices and weather channels are not
changed here.

---
diff --git a/net/wireless/mlme.c b/net/wireless/mlme.c
--- a/net/wireless/mlme.c
+++ b/net/wireless/mlme.c
@@ -1338,6 +1338,11 @@ cfg80211_start_background_radar_detection(struct cfg80211_registered_device *rdev,
 	cac_time_ms = cfg80211_chandef_dfs_cac_time(&rdev->wiphy, chandef);
 	if (!cac_time_ms)
 		cac_time_ms = IEEE80211_DFS_MIN_CAC_TIME_MS;
+	/* Adjacent 52-64 CAC is off-channel in the ETSI region. */
+	if (reg_get_dfs_region(&rdev->wiphy) == NL80211_DFS_ETSI &&
+	    chandef->width == NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_80 &&
+	    chandef->center_freq1 == 5290)
+		cac_time_ms = max(cac_time_ms, 360000U);
 
 	rdev->background_radar_chandef = *chandef;
 	rdev->background_radar_wdev = wdev; /* Get offchain ownership */
